# Firebase web app config — Firebase Console → Project settings → General → Your apps,
# or: firebase apps:sdkconfig WEB --project <project-id>
#
# The real values for the "storybridge-eb71e" project are committed in .env.production
# (they are public identifiers, not secrets — see apps/cms/.env.production for the same
# reasoning). Copy this file to .env.local only when pointing the site at a different
# Firebase project.
#
# The website only ever reads Firestore (published articles — see src/lib/articles.ts),
# never writes, and has no Auth or Storage dependency — so it needs fewer of these than
# the CMS does.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=storybridge-eb71e
